For $0\le x<3$:
$\begin{align*}F(x)&=\int_0^x\frac16\,dt\\&=\frac x6.\end{align*}$
The probability accumulated up to $3$ is $F(3)=\frac12$.
For $3\le x\le5$:
$\begin{align*}F(x)&=\frac12+\int_3^x\frac14\,dt\\&=\frac12+\frac{x-3}4\\&=\frac{x-1}4.\end{align*}$
Thus
$F(x)=\begin{cases}0,&x<0,\\\dfrac x6,&0\le x<3,\\\dfrac{x-1}4,&3\le x\le5,\\1,&x>5.\end{cases}$
Both pieces give $F(3)=\frac12$, and $F(5)=1$.
